{
  "_comment": [
    "The work a part can have done on it to take its mileage off (see docs/modding.md, \"rebuilds.json\"). A job is for the",
    "parts of its kinds (work_order.json's) or of its groups (part_groups.json's shelves). way: kit (the player's own work)",
    "or exchange (swapped at the parts counter for a rebuilt one, the old part the core). restores: the condition the part",
    "is in after it, 0 to 1 (a kit is not a new part); min_wear: a part worn below it is too far gone for the job (it wants",
    "a machine shop); cost: the kit or the rebuilt unit, a share of the part's new price, never less than cost_at_least",
    "dollars; minutes: the work, or the trip to the counter; off: done with the part off the car and off any other part",
    "(on the shelf, or the engine on the stand); bare: done with nothing mounted on it; fixes_damage: takes its damage off",
    "too. The player reads rebuild.<id> in the text, else name. A mod's job of the same id takes the place of this one,",
    "whole; \"disabled\": true takes it out.",
    "roll: how far under restores the work may land (0 to 0.5; left out, 0.08 for a kit, none for an exchange unit, 0.02 at",
    "a machine shop): the player's own work comes out a little rough now and then, never worse than the part was.",
    "",
    "way machine: left at a machine shop, back in days. cut: what it cuts (bore, grind, mill...); each time the part goes",
    "to the next of sizes, and past the last it cannot be cut again (no cut: the job takes no metal off and can be done",
    "again). A size: id, say, figures (the engine figures it changes from then on, as a part pack's \"figures\": add to the",
    "bore, times the chamber...) and worth (the part's worth at that size against the factory's; speed work needs none: an engine is priced by its dyno power). restores 0 with a cut:",
    "the part's wear is left as it is (speed work). fits_new: a kind the machinist fits new to suit the cut (pistons for a",
    "bore; the part's own swapped, or the block's stock set when it has none), in the price at fits_new_cost of their new",
    "price; those parts and the cut part only go together at the same size. any_size: made to any size the part is not",
    "(new pistons for a block bored before). speed: speed work, listed apart. The player reads rebuild.<id>.size.<size>",
    "and rebuild.<id>.done (\"bored {size}\") in the text."
  ],
